; 05-replay-numbers: the place an error made right after a library function's call says it was made (y, unbound, the
; next argument), when the call's value is its native's: each function called through one call (unpack's), three
; times with some arguments (its code runs, then its native's value is used, with the place its code left), then with
; others, which may go the same way or another (floor of positive, negative and whole values in turn ...)
(fun {probe g args bind} {do (if bind (set y 0) NIL) (list (unpack g args) y)})
(fun {run g l} {map (fn {p} {probe g (fst p) (snd p)}) l})
